<!-- Thank you for trying to improve Rust through the RFC process! -->
<!-- Please add a short summary of your RFC below -->

Change closure capture inference rules for `Copy` captures, allowing more code to compile without changing semantics for existing closures.

Some examples of closures that would start compiling:

```rust
fn callable(c: char) -> impl Fn() -> char {
    || c
}
```

```rust
fn main() {
    let cs: u32 = (0..0xCC).flat_map(|c| (0..c).map(|cc| c + cc)).sum();
    assert_eq!(cs, 4203318);
}
```

Implementation: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/163717

